* The airlock's door interlock (openc2e Creatures 2 project, our own script).
* Run by openc2e after the world loads (Additions folder); safe to repeat.
*
* The interlock (owner, 2026-11-11: the two doors must never be open
* together). Each door's own script, opening, shuts the other door and
* drains or floods the chamber, waiting between steps, and marks itself open
* (OV00 0) only at the end; a press of the other door in that window found
* this one still "shut" and opened too, leaving both open. A guard (2 1 153,
* invisible) looks twice a second: with both doors open, it shuts the one
* that does not fit the water (the land door when the chamber is flooded,
* drain machine OV00 0; the sea door when it is drained, OV00 1), using
* that door's own script.
enum 2 1 153 kill targ next
inst new: simp blnk 1 0 0 0 setv cls2 2 1 153 setv attr 16 mvto 5000 1320 tick 5 slow
scrp 2 1 153 9
  setv var0 1 setv var1 1 setv var2 0
  enum 2 9 7 setv var0 ov00 next
  enum 2 9 8 setv var1 ov00 next
  enum 2 3 4 setv var2 ov00 next
  doif var0 eq 0
    doif var1 eq 0
      doif var2 eq 0
        enum 2 9 8 mesg writ targ 0 next
      else
        enum 2 9 7 mesg writ targ 0 next
      endi
    endi
  endi
endm
